  "description": "Draw a protein, enzyme or antibody as a cartoon (ribbon diagram).\n\nFetches its structure from the PDB (AlphaFold model if there is none) and\nwrites PNG/SVG files plus a rotatable panel: helices as spirals, strands as\narrows, bound groups such as heme or zinc as sticks. Works for enzyme and\nprotein names (lysozyme, trypsin, hemoglobin, insulin), gene symbols\n(RecA), antibody INNs (trastuzumab) and a plain \"antibody\" or \"IgG\".\nAntibodies come with the IgG domain scheme; an antibody without a known\nstructure shows the architecture of an intact IgG. A protein's 3D\nstructure is this tool too — the panel rotates.\n\nNot this tool for: a small molecule, a peptide sequence or any skeletal\nformula (use generate_molecule); a small molecule as a 3D model (use\ngenerate_3d); a protein's function, EC number or cofactors as text (use\nlookup, topic \"biochem\").\n\nArgs:\n    name: English protein, enzyme, gene or antibody name (\"lysozyme\",\n        \"trastuzumab\", \"antibody\"); an organism may follow (\"human\n        lysozyme\").\n    formats: \"png\", \"svg\" (default both). A cartoon has no CDXML.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "properties": {
      "formats": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "type": "array"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ],
        "default": null,
        "title": "Formats"
      },
      "name": {
        "title": "Name",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "name"
    ],
